KNOWNBUG
main.cpp
--cpp17
^\[main\.assertion\.1\] line \d+ braced default member initializer of scalar: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.2\] line \d+ WRONG must FAIL: FAILURE$
^VERIFICATION FAILED$
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
^CONVERSION ERROR$
--
N5008 [dcl.init.list]/3.9: list-initializing a scalar from a single-element
braced-init-list initializes it from that element, so `int x{42};` as a default
member initializer sets the member to 42.  CBMC leaves the braced-init-list
unconverted for a scalar member's default member initializer; the raw
initializer_list reaches GOTO conversion and aborts the bit-vector flattener
(boolbv_widtht::get_entry).  `int x = 42;` works.  Separate bug found while
fixing the class-typed default-member-initializer case; tracked so it is not
lost.  Flip to CORE once the single-element braced-init-list is unwrapped for
scalar members.
